      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_2",
      "quote": "Purpose There is currently no consensus on nonoperative management in adult patients after a stable type B ankle fracture.",
      "reason": "The review’s rationale is grounded in the current state of knowledge by explicitly stating there is no consensus on nonoperative management for stable type B ankle fractures."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_2",
      "quote": "The aim of this review is to compare a removable orthosis versus a cast regarding safety and functional outcome in the NOM of stable type B ankle fractures.",
      "reason": "The need to conduct the review is explained through the stated aim to resolve safety and functional outcome uncertainty by comparing the two nonoperative approaches."
    },
